%% Sequence 02d — Routed task assignee edit
%% Updated: 2026-07-27.
%% Scenario: a project manager assigns, reassigns, or clears an assignee through task edit.
%% Evidence status: Implemented. Dedicated AssignTaskCommand/RevokeTaskAccessCommand have no active HTTP route.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor PM as Project manager
    participant UI as «boundary» tasks/edit.svelte
    participant C as «boundary» EditTaskController
    participant K as «control» UpdateTaskCommand
    participant P as «control» Task permission + assignee rules
    participant D as «entity» PostgreSQL
    participant E as «control» Post-commit effects

    PM->>UI: Select assignee or clear current assignee
    UI->>C: PUT /tasks/:taskId { assigned_to }
    activate C
    C->>K: execute(taskId, UpdateTaskDTO)
    activate K
    K->>D: Lock task and load organization/assignee facts
    activate D
    D-->>K: Task, membership, contributor context
    deactivate D
    K->>P: canUpdateTaskFields() + validateAssignee()
    activate P
    P-->>K: Allowed or policy violation
    deactivate P
    alt Assignment edit denied
        K-->>C: Policy violation
        C-->>UI: Validation/authorization error
    else Assignment edit allowed
        K->>D: Update tasks.assigned_to and write version/audit rows
        activate D
        D-->>K: Updated task record
        deactivate D
        Note over K,D: Routed edit does not create a task_assignments row
        K->>E: Publish update, invalidate cache, notify affected assignee
        activate E
        E-->>K: Effects handled
        deactivate E
        K->>D: Load current task detail
        D-->>K: Task detail
        K-->>C: Current task detail
        C-->>UI: 200 response or redirect
        UI-->>PM: Updated assignee shown
    end
    deactivate K
    deactivate C
